d production practices including sanitation.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite or corequisite: FDSC 4500/VIEN 4500.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment preference given to: Viticulture and Enology majors.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": ["Describe and differentiate traditional red, white, sparkling, and dessert winemaking methods and styles and understand the regulations which control them.", "Describe and distinguish the technological and equipment options for wine and grape processing.", "Describe the impact of winemaking methods on water and energy usage and on waste generation.", "Explain and describe the administrative and regulatory challenges related to winemaking.", "Describe, recognize, and list common causes and control measures for microbiological, chemical, and physical wine spoilages.", "Evaluate sanitation in the winemaking environment and relate it to impacts on wine quality.", "Identify and select appropriate chemical and microbial controls and limits to monitor and control the winemaking process."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AG", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2769, "crseId": 369698, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "VIEN", "catalogNbr": "4650", "titleShort": "Wine Microbiology", "titleLong": "Wine Microbiology", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 2947, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "10:20AM", "timeEnd": "11:10AM", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/16/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "pag235", "firstName": "Patrick", "middleName": "",